---Model that represents the properties of the scenario.
---@class azure.chaos.ScenarioProperties
---@field provisioningState? azure.chaos.ProvisioningState Most recent provisioning state for the given scenario resource.
---@field createdFrom? string Resource ID of the template version this scenario was created from (optional). The ID has the form `/providers/Microsoft.Chaos/scenarioTemplates/{scenarioTemplateName}/versions/{version}`. This property retains its existing string representation for compatibility with earlier API versions and SDKs. A scenario's structure comes from exactly one of two mutually exclusive sources. When `createdFrom` is supplied on create, the referenced template version is the authoritative source for the scenario's structure; inline `parameters` and `actions` are not used. When `createdFrom` is absent, the structure comes from the inline `parameters` and `actions` supplied in the request. Supplying neither source is rejected by request validation.
---@field version? string Version of the scenario, supplied by the author. Defaults to `1.0` when not supplied on create. This is the scenario's own version and is independent of the version of any template it was created from.
