---Model that represents a built-in scenario template. A scenario template is a versioned,
---read-only blueprint published by Microsoft that can be used to create a scenario. Templates
---are the same shape as the scenarios they produce, so an action read from a template is valid
---input to a scenario create.
---
---The template is addressed without a version, and always describes its newest published
---version. Address a specific version through the child versions resource.
---@class azure.chaos.ScenarioTemplate
---@field id? string Fully qualified resource ID for the resource. E.g. "/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/{resourceProviderNamespace}/{resourceType}/{resourceName}"
---@field name? string The name of the resource
---@field type? string The type of the resource. E.g. "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines" or "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"
---@field systemData? azure.chaos.SystemData Azure Resource Manager metadata containing createdBy and modifiedBy information.
---@field properties azure.chaos.ScenarioTemplateProperties The properties of the scenario template's newest published version.

