---A customer-managed key reference, not key material.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyEncryption
---@field keyEncryptionKeyUrl string The versionless HTTPS Key Vault key URI in the supported cloud and Workspace tenant. The key vault must belong to the same Microsoft Entra tenant as the Workspace. Its HTTPS origin must match the vault referenced by keyVaultResourceId. The service validates the effective pair and caller vault-read permission synchronously through Azure Resource Manager before creating public operation metadata, accepting the configuration operation, persisting requested encryption, or changing Storage or customer data. Supports RSA keys in Azure Key Vault and RSA-HSM keys in Premium Key Vault, with key sizes of 2048, 3072, or 4096 bits. Premium RSA-HSM keys use the same vault URL. The separate Azure Managed HSM service is not supported; Managed HSM endpoints are rejected before operation acceptance. A key version, query string, or fragment is not permitted. Azure Storage follows key versions automatically. Keep the previous version available for at least 24 hours after rotation.
---@field keyVaultResourceId string The fully qualified Azure resource ID of the key vault that contains the key. Use /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/{vaultName}, not a key child resource, Managed HSM, or URL. Full PUT with CMK and PATCH that changes either CMK member require Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/read on the effective vault. The service compares its canonical ID, tenant, and vault URI with the requested pair before accepting the operation.

---A partial customer key reference, validated after merging with the stored setting.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyEncryptionPatchMergePatchUpdateOrCreate
---@field keyEncryptionKeyUrl? string|distilled.Null The replacement versionless key URI. Omission retains the URI; null deletes it. A same-vault replacement retains the stored vault ID. The effective pair is authorized and validated before acceptance; an incomplete or mismatched pair is rejected. Key path and name casing is preserved.
---@field keyVaultResourceId? string|distilled.Null The vault resource ID to merge with the key URL. Omission retains the ID, but does not bypass caller authorization when the URL changes. Null deletes the ID; a remaining CMK object without both members is invalid. Changing vault requires a coherent new URL and ID pair.

---The service application that the customer authorizes to use the key.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyOnboarding
---@field applicationId string The Microsoft Entra application ID used for customer consent, returned for existing Workspaces, including Microsoft-managed Workspaces. This does not permit adding CMK to an existing Microsoft-managed Workspace. Before creating a Workspace with a customer key, obtain the application name and ID for the target cloud from the service onboarding documentation or Portal, then consent and grant key access. The configuring caller separately needs Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/read on the referenced vault. GET returns the same application ID. This is not a service principal object ID or an identity selector. The Workspace's top-level identity does not select this application.

