---Two independent partitions of expanded scope occurrences after normalized-scope deduplication. Distinct service groups remain distinct even if their members coincide. The known/unknown counts and the four completeness counts each sum to totalCount.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceDiscoveryScopeCoverageSummary
---@field totalCount number The number of expanded Azure Resource Manager scope occurrences represented by the result.
---@field knownExpectedSetCount number The number of scopes with an authoritative complete expected resource-occurrence set, including authoritatively empty sets.
---@field unknownExpectedSetCount number The number of scopes whose complete expected inventory set is unavailable. A service group's known subscription or resource-group membership does not establish its descendant-resource denominator.
---@field establishedCount number The number of scopes with Established coverage.
---@field baselineUnknownCount number The number of scopes with a structurally unavailable denominator and no observed shortfall, including successful observed-empty container scans.
---@field verificationIncompleteCount number The number of scopes with required verification failure, unavailable required child enumeration, or a proven accessible required resource absent from the snapshot.
---@field knownPartialCount number The number of scopes with confirmed undelivered obligations and no remaining system-verification gap.

