---The validated requested key and vault reference, onboarding information, and service observations.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceEncryption
---@field customerManagedKeyEncryption? azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyEncryption The requested customer-managed key. Its presence is fixed by accepted Workspace creation: adding CMK to a Microsoft-managed Workspace or removing CMK from a CMK-created Workspace is rejected with InvalidEncryptionConfiguration. The key pair remains updateable on CMK-created Workspaces, including after a failed creation. A present object requires a coherent keyEncryptionKeyUrl and keyVaultResourceId pair. After synchronous caller and vault validation, the accepted pair can be returned while configuration is Pending. It does not prove that active data already uses the requested key.
---@field customerManagedKeyOnboarding? azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyOnboarding The service application to authorize before creating a new CMK Workspace; also returned for existing Workspaces.
---@field status? azure.chaos.WorkspaceEncryptionStatus The observed result, separate from the requested setting.

---The validated requested key and vault reference, onboarding information, and service observations.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceEncryptionInput
---@field customerManagedKeyEncryption? azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyEncryption The requested customer-managed key. Its presence is fixed by accepted Workspace creation: adding CMK to a Microsoft-managed Workspace or removing CMK from a CMK-created Workspace is rejected with InvalidEncryptionConfiguration. The key pair remains updateable on CMK-created Workspaces, including after a failed creation. A present object requires a coherent keyEncryptionKeyUrl and keyVaultResourceId pair. After synchronous caller and vault validation, the accepted pair can be returned while configuration is Pending. It does not prove that active data already uses the requested key.

---A partial encryption setting. Omitted fields are unchanged and null deletes a
---writable field. A remaining customerManagedKeyEncryption object must have a
---coherent key URL and vault resource ID. Read-only onboarding and status
---inputs are ignored. The accepted creation choice cannot change. Only a
---CMK-created Workspace can update the pair. Changing either member requires synchronous caller and
---vault validation of the merged pair, including any retained member.
---@class azure.chaos.WorkspaceEncryptionPatchMergePatchUpdateOrCreate
---@field customerManagedKeyEncryption? azure.chaos.WorkspaceCustomerManagedKeyEncryptionPatchMergePatchUpdateOrCreate|distilled.Null The customer key configuration to merge on a CMK-created Workspace. Null deletion is rejected on CMK and is a no-op only when already absent on a Microsoft-managed Workspace. An empty object retains an existing complete pair without a lookup when neither member changes, but is invalid when the merged pair is incomplete. Unsupported mode changes are rejected before vault lookup, operation creation, desired mutation, or Storage effects.

